From 322b8979887d48931c254bdd095cd2661e7ecfbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <226450061+logdog2325@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:05:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 159/161] XD Netplay: netplay multi battles, phase 1 (four
 seats, Multi format for testers, four machines in sync)

Multi rooms (format 9, listed only with MultiEnabled) seat joiners on ports
2, 3 and 4 by queue; seats hold while a start or a battle is on. Each seated
player's team goes to a private stage file; at Start the host writes four
boot copies (NetPlayTemp1-4) from its own port-2 save and the stages, the
server syncs exactly those and the host boots from them, so its real saves
are never written. Pad map {host, Seat 2, Seat 3, Seat 4}, four GBAs.

Port 1 in netplay: channel 0 travels in GC format with the GBA keys and a
control byte in the analog bytes. Only the host plans; a mode switch rides
the next channel-0 entry it pushes and every machine applies it at the pop of
that entry. A transfer in flight drains to the inner GBA. A socket-1 wait
counter (HLE start hook, read only) replaces the post-battle timing rules.

Lag: one room-wide buffer sized from the two slowest guests (cap 30), plus a
Multi-only chase re-anchor and edge-safe lower. Multi refuses Host Input
Authority, Golf and the mixed-arch safest override; runs single core.

Rules: Lv 100, Orre Colosseum bans and clauses per trainer, bring 6 pick 3.
Block: layout 3, pairing 0, Custom 1, no model lines, preview heads hidden.
MultiFillSeats (INI) lets two machines play all four seats. The preview
cancel pin (MultiPreviewCancelPin) stays off until its solo test passes.

Android: seat roles, Submit Team for seated players, and touch input on the
local pad of the visible GBA (also fixes 1v1 joiners).
